{
  "summary": "The experiment tested a baseline multimodal configuration combining RNA data encoded via PCA and image data via ResNet50 using simple concatenation fusion. Validation accuracy of 0.5266 suggests moderate performance, with validation F1 of 0.5104 supporting this trend. The result provides an initial observation for multimodal performance but does not isolate the impact of multimodality compared to single-modality baselines or other design choices."
}

